    # Open-source Software
    Open source software that are either authored/co-authored by me, or
    involved in the design/implementation of the software.
    Also included is a list of minor updates I have contributed to other
    open source software.

    # General Purpose Software
    ## [Sope](https://github.com/srirampc/sope)

    Rust library for MPI . Based to the C++ library
    [mxx](https://github.com/patflick/mxx), library provides a simplified, and
    type-safe bindings to common MPI operations with error handling.
    Also includes a collection of scalable, high-performance standard algorithms for
    parallel distributed memory architectures, such as sorting and distribution.
    Available at [github](https://github.com/srirampc/sope).

    ## [Awitree](https://github.com/srirampc/)

    A simple interface to [jstree](https://www.jstree.com/), javascript library
    to construct tree via the [AnyWidget](https://anywidget.dev/) protocol that
    can be used to render trees in both Jupyter and Marimo
    Notebooks. Source available at [github](https://github.com/srirampc/awitree)

    # Research Software (Role as Author/Co-author)

    ## [ParEnsNet](https://github.com/srirampc/parensnet_rs)
    Parallel Ensemble networks for large-scale single-cell data.
    Available at https://github.com/srirampc/parensnet_rs.

    ## [SCEMENT](https://github.com/AluruLab/scement)
    Software for scalable and memory efficient integration of large-
    scale single cell RNA-sequencing Data.
    Available at [github]https://github.com/AluruLab/scement.

    ## [Apache Airavata Cerebrum](https://github.com/apache/airavata‑cerebrum)
    A repository for the Integrated Neuroscience Computational
    Framework. Contributed to one of the components that allows
    integration of large single-cell datasets from Brain Atlases into
    Computational Neuroscience models.
    Available at [github](https://github.com/apache/airavata‑cerebrum).

    ## [EnGRaiN](https://github.com/AluruLab/EnGRaiN)
    EnGRaiN is the first supervised machine learning method to
    construct ensemble networks using small training datasets of
    true positives and true negatives among gene pairs. Available at
    https://github.com/AluruLab/EnGRaiN.

    ## [ParFastAAI](https://github.com/AluruLab/parfastaai)
    A C++ Implementation of a parallel algorithm for fast computation of
    Average Amino-acid Identity for bacterial and archeal genomes.
    Available at https://github.com/AluruLab/parfastaai.

    ## [gbrunner](https://github.com/srirampc/gbrunner)

    Utilities and runner scripts for generating gene regulatory net-
    works with arboreto, XGBoost and Light GBM. Available at
    https://github.com/srirampc/gbrunner.

    ## [Ardmore](https://github.com/AluruLab/ardmore)

    Ardmore is a suite of containers and aggregation scripts for sim-
    ulated runs that enables reproducibility in evaluation of gene
    network construction. Available at https://github.com/AluruLab/ardmore.

    ## [ADYAR](http://github.com/srirampc/adyar)

    ADYAR implements alignment-free heuristic for fast sequence
    comparisons with applications to phylogeny reconstruction.
    Available at http://github.com/srirampc/adyar.

    ## [ALFRED and ALFRED-G](http://srirampc.net/alfred)

    ALFRED implements an alignment free method to compute the
    average common substring measure with k mismatches, and is
    used for Phylogenetic Inference. ALFRED-G a greedy Align-
    ment Free Distance Estimator software for Phylogenetic Infer-
    ence, and implements an approximate algorithm that takes linear
    time. Both available [here](http://srirampc.net/alfred.html).
    It is based on the metric of average common
    substring computed as described in the research paper:
    [doi: 10.1089/cmb.2015.0217](https://doi.org/10.1089/cmb.2015.0217) .

    ## [Parallel kMCS](https://bitbucket.org/srirampc/bhavani/)

    Parallel kMCS implements an efficient parallel algorithm that
    given a database of strings, identifies all pairs of strings that
    have common substrings, while allowing a limited number
    of mismatches.
    Available at https://bitbucket.org/srirampc/bhavani/.

    ## [PSbEC](http://srirampc.net/psbec.html)

    PSbEC is a parallel spectrum-based error correction software for
    big genomic datasets. It can be used as framework to parallel-
    ize any spectrum-based error correction software. Available at
    http://srirampc.net/psbec.html.

    # Research Software (Role as an Advisor/Collaborator)

    ## [ramBLe](https://github.com/AluruLab/ramBLe)
    ramBLe is a parallel framework for Bayesian Network Learning.
    Available at https://github.com/AluruLab/ramBLe.
    This software is selected as one of the three finalists for for inclu-
    sion as a reproducibility challenge in the SC21 Student Cluster
    Competition (SCC).

    ## [ParsiMoNe](https://github.com/AluruLab/ParsiMoNe)
    Parallel implementation for construction of Module Networks.

    ## [MCPNet](https://github.com/AluruLab/MCPNet)
    MCPNet is a gene regulatory network (GRN) reconstruction tool that identify
    long range indirect interactions based on a novel metric called MCP Score.
    MCP score uses maximum-capacity-path, a graph theoretical measure, to
    quantify the relative strengths of direct and indirect gene-gene interactions.
    MCPNet is implemented in C++ and is parallelized for multi-core and
    MPI multi-node environments. It is designed to reconstruct networks in
    unsupervised and semi-supervised manners.

    # Other Open Source Contributions (Made Minor Updates/Bug-fixes)

    ## [hdf5-rust](https://github.com/srirampc/hdf5-rust)

    A fork of [metno/hdf5-rust](https://github.com/metno/hdf5-rust)
    that includes MPI parallel read/write of HDF5 1D/2D datasets.

    # [dualrnaseq](https://github.com/srirampc/dualrnaseq)

    A fork of [nf-core/dualrnaseq](https://github.com/nf-core/dualrnaseq)
    that enables long running quantification processes and fix annotation
    bugs.
